What are Air Dome Structures?
Air dome structures are lightweight, flexible architectural solutions constructed from high-performance fabric membranes that utilize continuous air pressure to maintain their shape. These innovative enclosures offer key advantages such as rapid deployment, cost efficiency, and versatility across a wide range of applications. Common configurations include single-layer and multi-layer designs, with materials typically featuring reinforced PVC, ETFE, or PTFE coatings engineered for long-term durability and thermal performance.
